Subject: Fail at load, not at call

What this does
  Fail at load, not at call.

Why we need it
  A function without a register program was created silently and threw `function was not lowered` at its first call, far from the cause; a blob carrying no register program loaded the same way.

What it adds
  `js_create_function` raises `InternalError` with the site's reason and the source position as soon as the scan leaves the function uncompiled; the reader rejects a zero register-program flag with `bytecode without a register program`; the call-time check stays as a backstop that says it is an engine bug; `REGVM_FORCE_DEFER` (knob builds) forces the path; the `QJS_REGVM_VERIFY` dead-end macro no longer needs `assert` to be compiled out.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
